BE-300 2.6.8.1: NAND MTD driver over the VRC4173 XFER engine.

Port of the 2.4.18 nand_be300.c (which follows the 4.2.9
board/casio-be300/nand.c): a plain mtd_info over the XFER engine at PA
0x0A00A4xx / 0x0A00B000 with the ptable/spl/kernel/rootfs partitions
written by tools/mk_be300_nand.py.  The JFFS2 root lives on mtd3.

Registered as MTD_NORFLASH: the emulator synthesizes Casio NANDWRITER
tags in OOB and drops OOB writes, so 2.6.8 JFFS2's NAND mode would read
every block as bad/unclean.  In NOR mode cleanmarkers stay in the data
area and OOB is never touched -- the behaviour 2.4.18 JFFS2 had.

